  <prompt>Author the full DS-2 §6.1 unit test suite against task 102's dispatcher: DispatchCoreDecisionTests (table-driven over every DispatchCoreAsync branch), DispatchIdempotencyService.cs + tests (Level-2 Redis lock, mirror of BFF IdempotencyService coverage incl. fail-open branches, lock TTL = MaxHandlerDuration not the BFF's 5-min default), HandlerEnvelopeRoundTripTests (enqueuer BodySerializerOptions serialize -&gt; dispatcher deserialize -&gt; identical envelope), and ReconcilerEnqueuePayloadAttemptTests (task 107's fix -- retry-path MessageId differs from original; first-enqueue MessageId stable across ticks).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in table-driven xUnit/NUnit test authoring, fake ServiceBus/Cosmos/Redis test doubles, and ADR-038 KEEP-path test architecture.</role>

  <goal>DispatchCoreDecisionTests covers all 11 branches from DS-2 §6.1's table (bad JSON, unknown id, processed-marker hit, lock-held, orphan run, terminal-status run, Success, Failure, handler-throws, applier-throws-below-max, applier-throws-at-max) using fakes for the keyed handler, IProvisioningRunRepository, and IHandlerOutcomeApplier. DispatchIdempotencyService exists (Core/Dispatch/) mirroring IdempotencyService.cs's shape against IDistributedCache, with the 30-min-scale TTL divergence documented. All tests pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-2 §6.1 enumerates the exact test matrix this task authors; DS-2 §4-L2 specifies DispatchIdempotencyService as a ~100-line intentional copy of the BFF's IdempotencyService.cs (L2 cannot reference the BFF assembly -- the same isolation rule as IProvisioningHandler.cs:8-13), keyed provisioning:idempotency:processed:{messageId} (24h TTL) and provisioning:idempotency:lock:{messageId} (TTL = DispatcherOptions.MaxHandlerDuration, since IDistributedCache offers no mid-flight lock renewal for a 30-60 min handler).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Dispatch/DispatchIdempotencyService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Dispatch/IDispatchIdempotencyService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Dispatch/DispatchCoreDecisionTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Dispatch/DispatchIdempotencyServiceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Dispatch/HandlerEnvelopeRoundTripTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/IdempotencyService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">DispatchCoreAsync must exist as the function under test</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests follow the 7 KEEP-path categories; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration-only tests, no ctor-null-check tests. DispatchCoreDecisionTests is a table-driven KEEP-path test over a pure decision function -- exactly the shape ADR-038 endorses.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-2 §4-L2">DispatchIdempotencyService lock TTL MUST equal DispatcherOptions.MaxHandlerDuration (NOT the BFF's 5-min default) since a 30-60 min handler holds the lock for its whole runtime with no mid-flight renewal on IDistributedCache. Fail-open on Redis outage, mirroring IdempotencyService.cs:43,96 -- L1 (SB dedup) + L3 (CompletedPhases scan) backstop it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dispatcher test suite</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
