    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Table-driven decision test" location="design-study-ds2-dispatcher-design.md §6.1">11-row table over DispatchCoreAsync branches; fakes for keyed handler, repository, applier -- no live SB/Cosmos/Redis required for this layer.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL, TEST-MODIFYING unconditional override). Read DS-2 §6.1 + §4-L2 in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="DispatchIdempotencyService">Author the class + interface mirroring IdempotencyService.cs's IsEventProcessedAsync/MarkEventAsProcessedAsync/TryAcquireProcessingLockAsync/ReleaseProcessingLockAsync shape, with the provisioning:-prefixed keys and MaxHandlerDuration-scoped lock TTL.</step>
    <step order="2" name="DispatchCoreDecisionTests">Author all 11 table rows per DS-2 §6.1 against fakes (keyed fake handler, in-memory IProvisioningRunRepository, recording IHandlerOutcomeApplier).</step>
    <step order="3" name="DispatchIdempotencyServiceTests">Mirror BFF's IdempotencyService test coverage against in-memory IDistributedCache incl. fail-open branches.</step>
    <step order="4" name="HandlerEnvelopeRoundTripTests">Serialize via the enqueuer's BodySerializerOptions, deserialize via the dispatcher's deserialization path, assert byte-identical envelope (guards the camelCase contract both sides depend on).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Attempt-field tests">Author ReconcilerEnqueuePayloadAttemptTests (depends on task 107 landing the attempt field) asserting retry-path MessageId differs from the original enqueue's MessageId, and first-enqueue MessageId stays stable across reconciler ticks (no attempt field present).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Run">dotnet test -- all new tests green; zero regressions in existing suite.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a DispatchCoreAsync branch from the DS-2 §6.1 table cannot be exercised without a live Service Bus/Cosmos connection (i.e., the pure-function boundary DS-2 §2.2 promised does not actually hold), STOP and escalate to task 102's owner rather than downgrading the test to an integration-only test -- the pure-function property is load-bearing for fast CI feedback on this class.</trigger>
  </escalation>

