  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">DispatchCoreDecisionTests contains &gt;=11 test cases matching the DS-2 §6.1 table rows; all pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">DispatchIdempotencyServiceTests verifies lock TTL is sourced from DispatcherOptions.MaxHandlerDuration (not a hard-coded 5-min value) via a config-override test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">HandlerEnvelopeRoundTripTests: enqueuer-serialized envelope deserializes to an object equal (by value) to the pre-serialization envelope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet test exits 0 for the full Dispatch/ test namespace.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- BFF's IdempotencyService is BFF-scoped and cannot be referenced from L2 (isolation rule per IProvisioningHandler.cs:8-13). Extension -- the ~100-line intentional copy is the documented pattern already used for the enqueuer/handler-contract (DS-2 §4-L2). Cost-of-doing-nothing -- without Level-2 idempotency, a redelivered message during lock-renewal failure re-invokes a 30-60 min handler with no distributed guard, relying solely on L1 (inert until task 108/C4.6 lands) and L3 (per-handler, not dispatcher-level).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-08-19. DispatchIdempotencyService.cs authored (Redis-backed via IDistributedCache,
    fail-open per DS-2 §4-L2, key format + TTL contract verbatim). DispatchModule.AddDispatchModule
    swapped from NoOpDispatchIdempotencyService to the real impl.

    Self-review (code-review + adr-check skills, Step 9.5) found + fixed 2 Critical ADR-038 violations
    in the first draft: (1) B4 banned constructor null-check tests -- removed; (2) B8 banned
    private-method/private-field reflection tests (HandlerEnvelopeRoundTripTests reflecting
    ServiceBusHandlerEnqueuer.BodySerializerOptions / ProvisioningHandlerDispatcher's
    BodyDeserializerOptions + TryDeserializeEnvelope) -- rewrote to test HandlerEnvelope's own public
    JSON contract instead; DS-2 §6.1 table row 1 ("bad JSON") is consequently NOT unit-tested at this
    layer (documented rationale in DispatchCoreDecisionTests.cs header) -- the class still exceeds the
    >=11 acceptance criterion via 11 real DispatchCoreAsync-exercised test methods (13 executed cases
    incl. Theory expansion) with zero reflection into private members.

    adr-check pass also surfaced a genuine design gap (not just a compliance nit): the original
    DispatchModule Redis-fallback silently degraded to same-instance-only in-memory cache in EVERY
    environment, including deployed multi-instance ones -- itself a silent-fail trap of the exact
    class this project exists to eliminate. Fixed by adding an IHostEnvironment parameter and gating
    the fallback to Development/Testing only (mirrors BFF CacheModule's isLocalLike carve-out);
    throws InvalidOperationException at startup in any other environment. AddDispatchModule's public
    signature changed (added IHostEnvironment param); Worker/Program.cs call site updated; new
    DispatchModuleTests.cs added to cover the gate.

    Final state: 787/787 L2 tests pass (0 regressions). Redis service registration confirmed via
    DispatchModuleTests.AddDispatchModule_RegistersIDispatchIdempotencyService_AsDispatchIdempotencyService.
    All 4 task-102 invariant tests still pass unmodified.
  </notes>
</task>
